Opening:
Students in {place} search for a ServSafe proctor every week. Most of them start with ServSafe's own search, which is out of date, clumsy and feels like it was built in 1980. They call the first few names, get disconnected numbers or no answer, then give up and search Google. That's where the big national training sites pick them up, and the local proctor never even knew they were looking.

I'm Gerald Miller, a ServSafe instructor and proctor for over 20 years. I built Find a Proctor so students can find active instructors and proctors in their ZIP code. I'm pleased to say it's the only real alternative to ServSafe's search, built with a modern feel and up-to-date options. You're already listed, and once you claim your listing, you'll stay there as long as you're active:

